{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement","id":838364,"title":"Transhumanist/\"Ordo Dracul-style\" Refinement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T19:22:35-08:00","id":838364,"title":"Transhumanist/\"Ordo Dracul-style\" Refinement","content":"&quot;I am not human, and I do not wish to be. Neither of these positions are wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;If your computer has a problem, do you destroy it? Do you get a whole new computer? Do you go back to using an abacus? No, you fix the problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I am not a perfect being. Many aspects of my current state are not desirable. But any human could say the same.&quot;<br /> <br /> Disquiet, Torment, and the Wasteland- these things are painful, destructive, and unenviable. All but the most twisted and broken Created long to escape them. But are mortality, aging, and illness much better? Yet the only road most Prometheans have to escape the problems of their condition leads inevitably to them. <br /> <br /> Or, to put it much more simply, what's wrong with being a robot? Why, a Promethean might wonder, does no one insist that R2D2 become human? Humans can clearly love robots.<br /> <br /> And why is humanity such an enviable condition anyway? Because humans do not cause Disquiet and Wastelands? But they have their own frailties. And humans aren't the only beings without those weaknesses. <br /> <br /> Basically, I'm working on a homebrew Refinement that's not based on becoming human, but on becoming a better Promethean. Those of this refinement do not wish to lose their artificial and inhuman natures, only the negative aspects of their condition, much like the Ordo Dracul. They obsessively study Pyros, Azoth, and all the other aspects of their existence, so that they can alter themselves to ward against Disquiet, Torment, and Wastelands. Their goals are to become something greater than human: immortal and powerful but capable of peaceful coexistence with humans. They also often seek out other supernatural creatures. The Ordo Dracul has worked with these Prometheans in the past, due to their similar philosophies. Many are drawn to other supernatural creatures, as well. They see the power and knowledge held by Changelings, Mages, and Demons, and wonder if these beings could aid them. After all, if someone can rewrite reality itself, could they not, say, suppress or reroute Disquiet? <br /> <br /> Members of the Refinement are split on humans. Some hold them in Centimani-like contempt. Others see no point in blaming them, and believe that humanity and mortality are valid paths, just not ones they personally would follow. <br /> <br /> Others, however, go farther. They wish to use their powers to aid humans by transforming them. Both humans and Prometheans are imperfect, so why should they not work together to improve each other, and overcome their respective frailties?<br /> <br /> This could actually be a really interesting Deviant backstory- modified by Prometheans to be more like them. Orrrrrrrr, a Demiurge might modify themself to better understand their creation. <br /> <br /> Now, the biggest obstacle is coming up with a name. <br /> <br /> Sadly necessary postscript: Please please please don't come into this thread to argue over whether or not it should be a thing. There are several threads for arguing over the Pilgrimage. This is for working on homebrew.<br /> <br /> EDIT: hoo boy hooooooooo boy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 02-28-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"ht