:{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:43:17-08:00","id":838385,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you don't like the topic of a thread, don't post in it.<br /> <br /> -Pendragon.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-27-2016, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:54:55-08:00","id":838393,"title":"","content":"On topic: OP, you're basically describing the Refinement of Lead, which exists and is in no way transhumanist, with a tiny dose of the Refinement of Quicksilver and the Hundred Handed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:02:17-08:00","id":838396,"title":"","content":"Also on topic: As a Promethean, you are metaphysically on fire. Redemption is putting out the fire. You can transmute all you want from that, but if you just try and change what you are, you are changing into something different that is still on fire. Sooner or later, you are going to die because you are on fire. I don't care how metaphysically transhuman and ascendant you are, you will burn. You will end. And your struggle to become more than human before you even know what it fucking means to be human will mean diddly shit if you are burnt to a crisp.<br /> <br /> Like, is that something people are missing? Transhumanism is a <i>human</i> pursuit. You cannot aspire to be better than human if you don't even fucking know what it means to be human. And if you know, <i>really know</i>, what it means to be human as a Promethean, congratulations, you've become a real boy and you can go get laser eyes and robot dicks and whatever. But for now?<br /> <br /> You are not human, and you are on fire. You don't even have the frame of reference, as a character, to know what you're aiming for, and every second you spend chasing that is another second you waste becoming so much char and ash.<br /> <br /> <i>you will burn, and no one will notice the ashes.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:05:09-08:00","id":838399,"title":"","content":"Alternatively; see my signature! Promethean is a game about becoming human, and neglecting that is akin to wondering why your Changeling has to have had a bad time in Arcadia or why your Mummy has to be from Irem - that's literally the premise of the game.<br /> <br /> Prometheans that don't want to become human already exist, and we call them Centimani. Not every Centimanus is a tentacled horror of a cartoon villain, they're literally just the Created that reject the quest for humanity and embrace their nature as something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:07:20-08:00","id":838400,"title":"","content":"TO be fair, you can have a good time in Arcadia. It just has to cost you something on returning.<br /> <br /> Pevensies from Narnia are totally viable characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:14:19-08:00","id":838402,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Good lord people, if you don't like the topic of a thread <b>DON'T FUCKING POST IN IT</b>! Just leave it alone, it's a big forum, there are plenty of other threads to read. I'm editing some of these posts for thread capping. No infractions...yet...consider this a global warning.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:16:36-08:00","id":838405,"title":"","content":"You don't want a Refinement, you want an Athanor.<br /> <br /> You can't be transhumanist if you aren't human. For a Promethean, becoming human <i>is</i> a transhumanist pursuit. You're literally thinking, feeling meat that's trying to become something metaphysically more than you are. And not just meat, but meat that is on fire. Yes, you can learn Disquietus and all of that, but you're still not solving your most pressing concern. And let's also not mince words here. You don't want to be &quot;transhuman&quot;, you just don't want to give up your superpowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:19:53-08:00","id":838407,"title":"","content":"So, Character dialogue moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You're really lucky, Sunny, you know that?&quot;<br /> &quot;How so, darling?&quot;<br /> &quot;You can't get sick. You never feel weak and shaky and cold and just-just so helpless.&quot;<br /> &quot;...I don't even know why that would be a problem. I don't even know <i>how</i> that's a problem.&quot;<br /> &quot;Ha. You're not missing out.&quot;<br /> &quot;Am I? I don't know how terrible it feels, so I might have some greener grass problems, but to me, it actually seems like...being sick is a good thing.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, shut up, Sunshine, you don't know what you're talking about.&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, yeah, we just talked about that. But, consider what I'm seeing. You've gone pale and sweaty and weak voiced, but you can still get up and move around if you have to-but you largely don't have to. Your work has let you stay home, your family has gone out of their way to make you feel comfortable and loved, letting you binge watch your shows-hell, they're even letting me come and cuddle you, and you know how they don't like that. You tell me you feel bad, but from my perspective, you're being pampered and given attention. You're getting what you want, and you're getting it while being with-together with your family. You receive love, as much as I can understand it, and that seems marvelous to me.&quot;<br /> &quot;Now, I remember why I love you. You still have no clue what you're saying, but you say the sweetest things anyways. You're always my sunshine.&quot; </div> </div> </div>THAT'S what a Promethean sees. Not feeling weak, not feeling limited, by an invisible enemy.<br /> <br /> They see being <i>in</i>. They see being <i>together</i>.<br /> <br /> THat's something they don't have. It seems more important than not being sick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:25:16-08:00","id":838412,"title":"","content":"We should really approach this as a Shard, because frankly what Geckopirateship is asking for <i>does</i> run counter to the premise of the game. But, counter to atamajakki's sig, if you're having fun playing the game in a way that violates its core premise, that's what matters. Now, on to the constructive feedback:<br /> <br /> 1) we don't know what 2e's Transmutations are like; but if they're anything like 1e's, atamajakki is right: Lead's Transmutations (I forget the name) are Promethean's \u201cOrdo Dracul\u201d Transmutations. Consider treating the Transhumanists as a Centimani-like \u201cRefinement\u201d that provides the Transmutations currently unique to Lead as well as Pandoran Transmutations (assuming they're still a thing in 2e). It's not <i>really</i> a Refinement, because it doesn't advance your Pilgrimage (unless you choose to rewrite 2e's Pilgrimage); but providing a means to downplay what sucks about being a Promethean while also granting a way to gain nifty mutations that humans don't get sounds just like what a Transhumanist would seek. <br /> <br /> 2) Making humans more like Prometheans will be covered in 2e; but it will be covered by the alchemists. I could definitely see a Promethean/Deviant crossoverchronicle where alchemists serve as the antagonists\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-27-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:31:47-08:00","id":838416,"title":"","content":"Though, to address what appears to be a core point, the Refinement of Silver seems like it could contribute to this idea, alongside Lead. In either case, I could see the idea of a Promethean trying to find a way to ensure his Redeemed self could gain powers similar to the ones they had as a Created after becoming human. Maybe something to do with studying Alchemists, figuring out a way to do the things they do without using Vitrol, or maybe hunting down a Psychic Vampire or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:41:20-08:00","id":838419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838412#post838412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lead's Transmutations (I forget the name)</div> </div> </div> </div>Saturninus, for the record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:42:53-08:00","id":838421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838405#post838405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't want a Refinement, you want an Athanor.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/prometheaninto-the-furnace/\" target=\"_blank\">Are you sure about that?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-28-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:45:41-08:00","id":838424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838419#post838419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saturninus, for the record.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plumbum, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:46:24-08:00","id":838425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838416#post838416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, to address what appears to be a core point, the Refinement of Silver seems like it could contribute to this idea, alongside Lead. In either case, I could see the idea of a Promethean trying to find a way to ensure his Redeemed self could gain powers similar to the ones they had as a Created after becoming human. Maybe something to do with studying Alchemists, figuring out a way to do the things they do without using Vitrol, or maybe hunting down a Psychic Vampire or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm\u2026 I don't really see that. Spiritus is about interacting with other Nightfolk; it's not really about becoming like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-27-2016, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:47:40-08:00","id":838427,"title":"","content":"Plumbum is the Refinement; Saturninus is the Transmutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T21:16:51-08:00","id":838441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838399#post838399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively; see my signature! Promethean is a game about becoming human, and neglecting that is akin to wondering why your Changeling has to have had a bad time in Arcadia or why your Mummy has to be from Irem - that's literally the premise of the game.<br /> <br /> Prometheans that don't want to become human already exist, and we call them Centimani. Not every Centimanus is a tentacled horror of a cartoon villain, they're literally just the Created that reject the quest for humanity and embrace their nature as something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing- Frankenstein's monster is my favorite &quot;classic monster&quot;. At its core, Promethean is Frankenstein: The Game. And I don't think it's being true to the core of that story. Basically, I want to like Promethean. I want to be able to play Promethean. I made this thread because I like the central premise of Promethean and want to have more options than what canon offers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T21:32:13-08:00","id":838451,"title":"","content":"Okay. Fair enough.<br /> <br /> *backs out*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:13:21-08:00","id":838466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838441#post838441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing- Frankenstein's monster is my favorite &amp;quot;classic monster&amp;quot;. At its core, Promethean is Frankenstein: The Game. And I don't think it's being true to the core of that story. Basically, I want to like Promethean. I want to be able to play Promethean. I made this thread because I like the central premise of Promethean and want to have more options than what canon offers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is similar to how some don't like spirits in <b>Werewolf</b> or hypertech in <b>Demon</b>. Full disclosure: I personally have no interest in playing <b>Promethean</b> without tye Pinocchio Complex; so I don't see myself using this Shard. That said\u2026<br /> <br /> Not having seen a preview of Pilgrimage (yet?), I can't say for certain what you're going to have to change here; but I'm pretty sure you're going to have to change <i>something</i>. Likewise, the existing Refinements and their Roles are built around the notion of trying to become human; from what I gather, the various Roles largely comprise a set of various aspects of the human condition that the Promethean is seeking to understand. So you're either going to want to rewrite te way Refinements and Roles work, or you're going to want to adapt the way the non-Refinement of Flux works. Given that your stated goal involves the Promethean remaining a Promethean, just \u201cbetter\u201d, you probably don't want to mess with the New Dawn business; that's about transforming yourself into not-a-Promethean. <br /> <br /> That said, I gather that the Centimani are going to have difficulties in 2e based on the premise that they're inherently unstable and not making any effort to stabilize themselves. For your stated goal of \u201cI want to do away with the flaws of being a Promethean while keeping the benefits\u201d, you may need to change the way Centimani are handled in 2e; or you may just need to expand on Saturninus with a few Transmutations tailored to deal with the difficulties Centimani face. <br /> <br /> Frankly though, I can't provide more detailed advice until we know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:20:33-08:00","id":838472,"title":"","content":"I would actually just chop out or severely diminish Disquiet and Wasteland, and perceive the refinements as modes of excellence. The material's there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:25:21-08:00","id":838474,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to be hostile when I repeat this, but what do these guys offer that Plumbum/Mercurius/Centimani don't? Plumbum has the &quot;understand the Created condition and make its flaws more manageable,&quot; Mercurius has &quot;learn from other supernaturals,&quot; and the Centimani have &quot;reject the Pilgrimage and embrace not being human.&quot; Other than the word 'transhumanism,' I'm not sure what some combination of those three doesn't cover what you want out of this concept.<br /> <br /> If it's the less philosophical and more physical side of transhumanism you want, then the Wretched can already swap their limbs around to alter their capabilities and the Unfleshed pretty soundly include any sort of technological bent.<br /> <br /> With all these in mind, I'm not sure what's left for you to want other than an unrelated beef with the canon idea of the New Dawn, which doesn't really have anything to do with a new Refinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-28-2016, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:32:19-08:00","id":838476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838474#post838474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mercurius has &quot;learn from other supernaturals,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mercurius has &quot;learn about alchemy and the Pyros.&quot; &quot;Learn from other supernaturals&quot; is Argentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:34:44-08:00","id":838477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838472#post838472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually just chop out or severely diminish Disquiet and Wasteland, and perceive the refinements as modes of excellence. The material's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean just not have Prometheans have those aspects? Or have the alternate New Dawn just get rid of them?<br /> <br /> I would have preferred that those mechanics be different or not exist, yes, but what I'm interested in isn't so much changing canon as working with it. I'm not saying, &quot;what if disquiet didn't exist&quot;, because canon directly contradicts that. I am saying, what if a group of Prometheans wanted to get rid of it without becoming human, and would they be able to work something out? That's something that doesn't require as much alteration of canon to work in, and it's something that can coexist with existing canon.<br /> <br /> And I actually would want the alternate New Dawn to be more complicated than that. The thing is, and I should have made it clearer that this wasn't my intention, I don't want the game to be &quot;Prometheans do the magic ritual and become super-robots and everything's perfect&quot;. This alternate path I'm working on should be hard. It requires sacrifice. The opening post was meant to be more of a description of the most idealistic aspirations of its adherents. <br /> <br /> As others have noted, WoD monsters aren't so much better than humans as different (personally, I think that this is why Mage and Beast have been so controversial: they haven't always handled this well). So becoming a...what are we calling them? What are we calling this whole New New Dawn? Whatever. Doing it should be a trade. The Promethean has to give something up. It's a hard road, harder than becoming human. <br /> <br /> That's something else I want to emphasize- something I dislike is how so many defenses of the Pilgrimage make being human sound so perfect and wonderful and euphoric and so on. Not just because it's not really true, because it makes the game seem like...just, like, everything sucks, you bust your ass becoming human, then, ding! Adventure over, everything's perfect! <br /> <br /> This alternate New Dawn isn't about that. Behind all the idealism and shiny robot dreams, it's an uncertain future. It's not having a definite end. It's not knowing when you'll be able to say &quot;this is enough&quot;. That's hard. But, and here's what I would emphasize if I were writing it, it's worth it. It's a good fight. Seeking knowledge, breaking barriers, improving yourself, questioning everything up to the very laws of reality- there's nobility in it. <br /> <br /> Back to gameplay, I really do want the New New Dawn to be a trade. For example, one idea I like is that it becomes harder or even impossible to conceal your true appearance, even when not using Pyros. That's something you have to sacrifice. It's about accepting that you are a living statue, and that it's fine to be a living statue- so you kind of can't really do that well at not looking like a living statue.<br /> <br /> Edit: About the other refinements- the problem is that, if what I've heard about 2e is accurate, they're all ultimately about becoming human and mortal. And the Centimani are being de-emphasized as a player option, and what I've seen seems to be, sadly, making them more cartoon villain-y and less &quot;a strange and disturbing path, but one that might be valid&quot;. And about the difference, the Centimani are about revelling in being a monster, and most importantly seem to have some level of hostility towards humanity. This refinement would have some space for contempt, but mostly it either supports ambivalence towards or compassion for humanity. <br /> <br /> And more gameplay ideas about the New New Dawn: I like the idea that it makes initial social interactions harder but pays off in the long run. So if someone meets you, they know right away something's off about you. They know you're a living statue or a robot or whatever. And that's a pretty big social penalty. But because there's no disquiet hanging over their head, they can move past that. Nothing stops them from realizing that even though you're a living statue, you're a kind, generous, and brave living statue that they can trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 02-28-2016, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:44:12-08:00","id":838480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838476#post838476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mercurius has &amp;quot;learn about alchemy and the Pyros.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Learn from other supernaturals&amp;quot; is Argentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all over the place tonight. Thank you, Satchel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:45:49-08:00","id":838481,"title":"","content":"Well, like, if I was going to have a transhumanist game of Promethean, I would soften the punches that make humanity seem like the big thing.<br /> <br /> I suppose the simplest solution, actually, would be to let you keep a lot of your features when you reach the New Dawn, just fuel them with Essence instead of Pyros, and be rid of the banes.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I'm spitting out ideas for a concept I don't even like as try to make amends for shitting all over the first page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:48:32-08:00","id":838484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838481#post838481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, like, if I was going to have a transhumanist game of Promethean, I would soften the punches that make humanity seem like the big thing.<br /> <br /> I suppose the simplest solution, actually, would be to let you keep a lot of your features when you reach the New Dawn, just fuel them with Essence instead of Pyros, and be rid of the banes.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I'm spitting out ideas for a concept I don't even like as try to make amends for shitting all over the first page.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we both succumbed to Torment there, Arc. I'm just gonna gently exit this thread.<br /> <br /> Apologies for my hostility, gecko.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:17:47-08:00","id":838493,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that as long as you're trying to develop something that's supposed to coexist in a game with Prometheans-as-written, you're going to run into problems. For instance: \u201cmonsters aren't better than humanity, so much as they're <i>different</i>.\u201d This is largely managed by the fact that monsters have flaws and weaknesses as well as strengths. Now take these \u201csuper-Prometheans\u201d that are the end goal of your alternate New Dawn (BTW, don't we already have a thread for that?): they retain all of the benefits of being a Promethean and none of the drawbacks (because having all of the benefits and a better capacity to manage the drawbacks doesn't require a New Dawn, just Saturninus). This makes them better than human \u2014 which is the whole point, as I understand it. <br /> <br /> So if there's a \u201cbetter than human\u201d endgame option out there, why would any rational and informed Promethean pursue the \u201chuman\u201d endgame? As I said in the other thread, I don't have a problem with non-human \u201cNew Dawns\u201d (become <i>qashmal</i>, become animal, become plant, etc.); I only have a problem with the \u201chave your cake and eat it too\u201d Promethean-without-drawbacks and similar alternatives \u2014 and even then only if you try to put them alongside \u201cbecome human\u201d in the same setting. <br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure you'll run into similar problems in other areas of the rules, because the game as written is calibrated to the notion that becoming human is desirable; so alternatives that are based on the notion that transhumanism is desirable will at the very least introduce cognitive dissonance, and very likely mechanical clashes. <br /> <br /> So I don't recommend trying to add transhuman options to the existing game; if you're going to try for transhumanism, you really should just change the game's calibration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:36:17-08:00","id":838504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838481#post838481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the simplest solution, actually, would be to let you keep a lot of your features when you reach the New Dawn, just fuel them with Essence instead of Pyros, and be rid of the banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a vague story idea built on something like this with the notion of a weird near-miss of the Aurora that effectively transferred the issues of the Disquieting aura to affecting the behavior of &quot;pure&quot; supernaturals like ephemeral beings as part of a bizarre extra leg of the Pilgrimage en route to finally inscribing the pattern of a soul into themself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T00:48:56-08:00","id":838532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838493#post838493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that as long as you're trying to develop something that's supposed to coexist in a game with Prometheans-as-written, you're going to run into problems. For instance: \u201cmonsters aren't better than humanity, so much as they're <i>different</i>.\u201d This is largely managed by the fact that monsters have flaws and weaknesses as well as strengths. Now take these \u201csuper-Prometheans\u201d that are the end goal of your alternate New Dawn (BTW, don't we already have a thread for that?): they retain all of the benefits of being a Promethean and none of the drawbacks (because having all of the benefits and a better capacity to manage the drawbacks doesn't require a New Dawn, just Saturninus). This makes them better than human \u2014 which is the whole point, as I understand it. <br /> <br /> So if there's a \u201cbetter than human\u201d endgame option out there, why would any rational and informed Promethean pursue the \u201chuman\u201d endgame? As I said in the other thread, I don't have a problem with non-human \u201cNew Dawns\u201d (become <i>qashmal</i>, become animal, become plant, etc.); I only have a problem with the \u201chave your cake and eat it too\u201d Promethean-without-drawbacks and similar alternatives \u2014 and even then only if you try to put them alongside \u201cbecome human\u201d in the same setting. <br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure you'll run into similar problems in other areas of the rules, because the game as written is calibrated to the notion that becoming human is desirable; so alternatives that are based on the notion that transhumanism is desirable will at the very least introduce cognitive dissonance, and very likely mechanical clashes. <br /> <br /> So I don't recommend trying to add transhuman options to the existing game; if you're going to try for transhumanism, you really should just change the game's calibration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did address this in a post I made in this thread, and it is a good point. I definitely want to make the &quot;New New Dawn&quot; a tradeoff. But I'm not sure whether I want it to be a single event- it might be better as a Coils of the Dragon-style progression, gradually getting better and better at mitigating Disquiet and the Wasteland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:00:44-08:00","id":838581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838396#post838396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>you will burn, and no one will notice the ashes.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: The Vigil.<br /> <br /> Hunters burn as well. Perhaps not as brightly, perhaps not as metaphysically, but they burn (out) all the same. Just like Hunters, perhaps some Prometheans think there are reasons worth burning for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:59:58-08:00","id":838626,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here's my deal. I'm all for it, but there's just one thing I'm pausing about.<br /> <br /> For me, writting fluff is easy. You can say anything you want. In fact, you've pretty much already covered all the fluff of the Refinement. So.... what exactly is left that you need help with your new Refinement for?<br /> <br /> In short, I mean mechanics. From the sounds of it, obsessive study of Pyros and reduction of Torment and Wastelands and Disquiet? We already have a pair of Transmutations that do that. Disquietism and Contamination. Maybe a touch of Volcanus. Seems pretty clear these are what you want.<br /> <br /> So... what exactly is left for you to do? Seems that pretty much everything is written down. I'm not sure what you need help with.<br /> <br /> Do you want some result of the New Dawn? I'm not sure that's necessary - the game ends once you hit the ND, and whatever happens after is immaterial to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:33:18-08:00","id":838712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838581#post838581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Counterpoint: The Vigil.<br /> <br /> Hunters burn as well. Perhaps not as brightly, perhaps not as metaphysically, but they burn (out) all the same. Just like Hunters, perhaps some Prometheans think there are reasons worth burning for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's....not the point of that line?<br /> <br /> If you die as a hunter, assumedly people will miss you, think of you. Prometheans don't have that due to disquiet. No one will give a shit when you, the Promethean, die.<br /> <br /> Now, on the whole? Sure, those look more congruent. But, you know, there's a distinction. Hunter set themselves on fire, and in fact can control how much they burn.<br /> <br /> Prometheans <i>don't</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, Hunters are clearly burning for something. What's a Promethean burning for? In their case, they are burning for their default state of existence. That's....a whole lot more pathetic.<br /> <br /> Anyways, no, not doing more in this thread, I'm threadcrapping enough as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T18:10:37-08:00","id":838889,"title":"","content":"Okay, wrote up some Stereotypes of other Refinements and supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Perspectives:<br /> <br /> Aurum: Can't you dream a bit bigger? Even the humans you so desperately want to mimic are hard at work trying to transcend their own limits. <br /> Cuprum: Contemplation and meditation are useful, I agree, but only as long as it motivates you. One should never settle- not for this state, and not for mortality. <br /> Ferrum: You believe in self-improvement, and that's admirable. We share that. But you we have somewhat higher goals than simply becoming muscular humans. <br /> Mercurius: Doesn't it seem odd that you study the wonders of Pyros and transmutations yet you ultimately plan to give them up?<br /> Stannum: You're angry, and you have every right to be. Why not do something with it, instead of just lashing out?<br /> Aes: It's admirable that you're so dedicated to helping your fellows. I'm just not sure you're leading them down the right path. <br /> Cobalus: You know the strengths and weaknesses of our condition well. Haven't you ever wondered if you could keep the first but the shed the second?<br /> Plumbum: We have some things in common, but not as many as you might think. We aren't so much in favor of coming to terms with our frailties as eliminating them.<br /> Argentum: You've seen the wonders of the world, you know that an existence beyond mortality is possible. Why not reach for it? I'd be happy to take a look at your research, too. <br /> Phosphorum: You dream of great things- have you ever considered that you might be able to accomplish them without blowing up?<br /> Centimani: I sympathize, and their way isn't entirely lacking in merit. Though I'm not sure how much all their rage will actually accomplish. <br /> Alchemists: Even in the worst among them, I can't help but see a certain nobility in their desire to improve and advance. I'm sure we can work out a mutually beneficial arrangement. <br /> <br /> Vampires: The ones who embrace their gifts and fight their limitations are worth knowing. The ones who wallow in self-pity and angst...even we aren't that insufferable. <br /> Werewolves: They're quite inhuman, really...but the world clearly has a place for them. Why can we not find our own?<br /> Mages: Why is humanity seen as an endpoint, when even humans have these beings as a higher state to aspire to? <br /> Changeling: They have known humanity and been ripped away from it- yet I've never heard of one becoming human, and I've only heard of a few who have tried. Even with their pain, they seem to be able to make peace with their condition. <br /> Hunters: Our kind don't usually get along well with them, but I don't begrudge them for defending themselves. <br /> Sin-Eater: They did get a rather good deal, and they seem to appreciate it. Though some of them need to realize that eventually you need to take a break from partying and get something done. <br /> Mummy: Quite like us, aren't they? Empowered and exalted in some ways, cursed and disadvantaged in others. Perhaps we can work together. I've heard that some seek immortality unhampered by their weaknesses...<br /> Demon: They seem to prove that humanity and immortal robot bodies aren't mutually exclusive. Plus, they seem useful to know, what with all the messing around with the secret machinery of reality that they do. <br /> Beast: Reveling in what you are without apology- there's something to be said for that. Still, they can be a bit...unruly, and I don't exactly share the contempt for human bravery and ingenuity that some of them seem to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:39:23-08:00","id":839205,"title":"","content":"I'm having an idea, combining this with some alternate-path ideas from other threads; forgive the brainspew but it might be helpful. Also I'm using the fire metaphor for Azoth/Pyros.<br /> <br /> So Prometheans are human in shape, but lack true souls; instead, they have a make-due of fire and change that slowly burns the world. Prometheans have two options now: try to be more human (and turn the fire into a soul), or remain as-is (and burn the world). What if there was a third option: shed the human form, become the fire? Maybe this means becoming a Quashmal, maybe something else, but it's a choice to head in the opposite direction from becoming human (as opposed to Centimanus, which doesn't promote changing what you are fundamentally). <br /> <br /> Of course, you want to have the fire banked in some way that lets you control what burns and what doesn't. But hey, we have beings of the Divine Fire that don't cause Torment: Qashmalim. But what's emphasized about those guys is how inhuman they are, how hard it is to understand them from a human perspective. So if a Promethean wants to have their fire, but bank it, too, they have to give up something else: their humanity.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Prometheans don't have humanity, they're learning it. But they have some of the pieces. They're trying parts on. But they're in a half-way state, half-fire, half-human. And fire is where the power comes from. So, on this road, you have to give up looking human, acting human, being human; get high enough and you start shedding Virtues and Vices, any sense of uniqueness and self. You're going to be more unsettling to start, and have harsher Disquiet as you begin down the path, as the fire eats up the human you could have been. But as you go, and have less human-bits, you ultimately overcome it: you're not trying to be human, so it's less disturbing when you aren't.<br /> <br /> So, mechanically, maybe there's a few path options (much like the Dragons): one that lets you lessen Disquiet (banking the fire), one that lets you shed humanity (feeding the fire), one that helps you understand the non-human side of your nature (contemplating the fire). You work on each of these paths, which have different Transmutations (borrowing probably from Lead, Mercury, and Centimanus, though not as a one-for-one). Starting down the path gives penalties to Disquiet and Wastelands, but those slowly decrease as you progress. Go far enough, you replace Humanity with something else, Qashmal-ity or something. It makes it much harder to interact with humans, as you are learning to be something that is inhuman. But ultimately, you can go far enough for your New New Dawn: becoming a creature that burns without consuming. (Which doesn't have to look like fire, you could be a statue or a robot or whatever; I just really like the fire metaphor.)<br /> <br /> ;tldr I think the goal of the Prommie Draculs should be becoming Qashmal or Quashmal-like: not human, but powerful. This requires them to slowly lose the things that make them human-like, like Humanity, Virtues, and Vices, replacing them with something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T11:17:53-08:00","id":839317,"title":"","content":"I feel like, &quot;use your condition to protect and guide humanity&quot;, or &quot;become a being that can better protect and guide humanity&quot; might work as either part of this Refinement or material for an entirely new one. The Qashmal idea fits with that, becoming literal guardian angels. I feel like a philosophical goal would be, to keep the alchemical theme, to &quot;reverse the equation&quot;- striving to live so that your existence benefits humanity more than it harms it. <br /> <br /> I want to emphasize a connection with humanity in this Refinement. We have Stannum and Centimani as Refinements for the Prommies who go full anti-human, I want this one to be more about coexistence- maybe even about helping humans change and progress along with Prometheans and eventually unifying the two into a whole with the best parts of each. <br /> <br /> I really do not like the demonization of alchemists that 2e looks like it's going to have, and that was part of the motivation behind these guys- they're far, far likelier to work with alchemists than fight them. &quot;Here, I'll make sure you have plenty of vitriol if I can use your lab.&quot; They might even work for a mixed chronicle- alchemists and Prometheans working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T11:56:47-08:00","id":839340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=839317#post839317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like, &quot;use your condition to protect and guide humanity&quot;, or &quot;become a being that can better protect and guide humanity&quot; might work as either part of this Refinement or material for an entirely new one. The Qashmal idea fits with that, becoming literal guardian angels. I feel like a philosophical goal would be, to keep the alchemical theme, to &quot;reverse the equation&quot;- striving to live so that your existence benefits humanity more than it harms it.<br /> <br /> I want to emphasize a connection with humanity in this Refinement. We have Stannum and Centimani as Refinements for the Prommies who go full anti-human, I want this one to be more about coexistence- maybe even about helping humans change and progress along with Prometheans and eventually unifying the two into a whole with the best parts of each.<br /> <br /> I really do not like the demonization of alchemists that 2e looks like it's going to have, and that was part of the motivation behind these guys- they're far, far likelier to work with alchemists than fight them. &quot;Here, I'll make sure you have plenty of vitriol if I can use your lab.&quot; They might even work for a mixed chronicle- alchemists and Prometheans working together.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Personally, I don't think the game works with having it both ways; you can either be human, or greater than human, but not both, hence why I emphasized becoming un-human. And it could be that having the best of both worlds is their noble shining goal, but no one's achieved it; they either find a semi-stable state as Prometheans, ignite into Qashmallim, turn off the path, or die. Part of it is that I see Wastelands/Disquiet being caused by trying to be both divine and mortal; the state is unbalanced, and that imbalance is inflicted on the world, and one must pick a side in order to balance that equation. That's all personal opinion, though, and I don't mean to say that it shouldn't or couldn't be done.<br /> <br /> Also, I should have emphasized the idea that Prometheans on this path can still be allied with humanity and working with/for them, despite not wanting to be them. (I can totally see some Prommies on this alt!Pilgrimage comparing it to animal rights activism, unfortunate implications included.) Dunno if I'd class Quashmallim as guardian angels, but some of them might be.<br /> <br /> Ooh, I agree about this being the allied-with-alchemists option, though. Particularly if you interpret Vitriol as the pieces of your learned humanity, you could literally give up what you learned in order to become something else. Of course, this only works as long as the alchemist doesn't try and take more than what is offered, and at some point the Promethean will run out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:17:05-08:00","id":839352,"title":"","content":"I think this Refinement might even have a Transmutation related to Vitriol, or an alternative way to generate it. I'm not suite sure if we've learned much about what it will be like in 2e, but we know alchemists need it to create potions that can truly change them, with immortality being listed as a sample of something they'd need it for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T13:07:02-08:00","id":839382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=839352#post839352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this Refinement might even have a Transmutation related to Vitriol, or an alternative way to generate it. I'm not suite sure if we've learned much about what it will be like in 2e, but we know alchemists need it to create potions that can truly change them, with immortality being listed as a sample of something they'd need it for.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an Athanor that generates it in the previews. On the one hand, if Vitriol is bits of humanity, I think it goes too strongly against the themes of the book to have it be creatable like that; on the other, the preview explicitly does just that (though it doesn't say at what rate/amount). Having a Transmutation line related to manipulating Vitriol, though, that would be pretty neat. Steal it back from those darned Pandorans, or those evil Centimani, or those rival alchemists, or that Throng that just doesn't seem to listen...<br /> <br /> Also I've realized some of my assumptions were wrong: Qashmallim <i>do</i> create Wastelands/Firestorms, so a Promethean wanting to avoid such negative aspects may not (initially) want to strive in that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T15:19:11-08:00","id":839468,"title":"","content":"Huh, I almost feel like we kind of have a plot hole here, in that if Vitriol is bits of humanity, it doesn't make that much sense thematically for it to be the thing that alchemists need to essentially make themselves inhuman. <br /> <br /> I feel like members of this refinement would definitely like having that athanor. <br /> <br /> Argh, we need a name so badly. Platinum? Silicon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T04:59:36-08:00","id":839804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=839317#post839317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to emphasize a connection with humanity in this Refinement. We have Stannum and Centimani as Refinements for the Prommies who go full anti-human,</div> </div> </div> </div>Stannum aren't anti-human. They are learning the lessons that can be taught by rage and torment, seeking to direct their fury in a productive manner. This is what divides them from the Centimani.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T07:59:41-08:00","id":839902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=839468#post839468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I almost feel like we kind of have a plot hole here, in that if Vitriol is bits of humanity, it doesn't make that much sense thematically for it to be the thing that alchemists need to essentially make themselves inhuman.<br /> <br /> I feel like members of this refinement would definitely like having that athanor.<br /> <br /> Argh, we need a name so badly. Platinum? Silicon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could be wrong in my interpretation of Vitriol, or it could be something different in 2e, IDK.<br /> <br /> In terms of names, I'm inclined against naming a metal, as the metal (and phosphorus) Refinements are paths towards becoming human. Maybe something inorganic, but not a metal? And if there's multiple Refinements, they could share a theme. Silicon could work. Maybe Jade or Diamond? I like the idea of gemstones, personally, although stones aren't refined, they're polished. But as an alternate to refining oneself into being human, one polishes ones flaws away, that kinda works as a metaphor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 03-01-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:32:13-08:00","id":840007,"title":"","content":"What about any of the noble gases? The Refinement of Argon has a nice ring to it (The Refinement of Krypton certainly has it's no-so-stealth-reference appeal as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:39:08-08:00","id":840014,"title":"","content":"You don't refine the noble gasses. They're completely inert.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest the refinement of Aluminium, which historically was incredibly difficult to refine/separate until a specific method was invented, and for a time it was more expensive and rarer than gold. For its Latin name, you can go with &quot;Luminum&quot; or something of the sort, which is an oblique reference to the Qashmallim and the Divine Fire in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T11:45:45-08:00","id":840068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840014#post840014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't refine the noble gasses. They're completely inert.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was the point: this \u201cRefinement\u201d (these \u201cRefinements\u201d?) doesn't advance your Pilgrimage toward a New Dawn; it makes it more comfortable to stay as a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:12:34-08:00","id":840132,"title":"","content":"All of those are pretty great. I might have to come up with multiple refinements just to find a place for all those great names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:00:43-08:00","id":840155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840068#post840068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that was the point: this \u201cRefinement\u201d (these \u201cRefinements\u201d?) doesn't advance your Pilgrimage toward a New Dawn; it makes it more comfortable to stay as a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>The name of the mechanic is <i>Refinement</i>. Your continued existence is untenable. Even if you seek to purge yourself from the weaknesses/disadvantages of the Promethean condition, you're still refining yourself into something. I'd argue that refining oneself into a Promethean Ubermensch-equivalent is a perfectly fine refinement, but the inert gas metaphor is not terribly appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:07:35-08:00","id":840159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840155#post840155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The name of the mechanic is <i>Refinement</i>. Your continued existence is untenable. Even if you seek to purge yourself from the weaknesses/disadvantages of the Promethean condition, you're still refining yourself into something. I'd argue that refining oneself into a Promethean Ubermensch-equivalent is a perfectly fine refinement, but the inert gas metaphor is not terribly appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thinking. I'm baffled by the insistence in 2e that anything other than progress towards humanity is &quot;stagnation&quot;, even progress towards other goals. So we should definitely keep the &quot;refinement&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> Edit: I might just go with Aluminum/Luminum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:50:45-08:00","id":840188,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Luminum is grammatically correct Latin (I think it may mean &quot;of the lights&quot; but I can't be sure). You may want to go with Lumen instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:11:20-08:00","id":840197,"title":"","content":"On a purely metaphysical level, I think that the problem with alternate New Dawns in Promethean, especially those that remove the weaknesses while retaining the strengths of the promethean condition is that the weaknesses derive from the strengths. The source of a Promethean's Transmutations, pseudo-immortality and all the other stuff is his Azoth, essentially a human soul burning too brightly to be contained. It is that very lack of containment that allows the promethean to work his transmutations and it is that which causes Disquiet and the Wasteland. Removing one requires removing the other. They are inseparable. A Promethean might learn new ways of accessing supernatural power, but as long as they use the Azoth, they will have to pay its price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:13:42-08:00","id":840198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840159#post840159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thinking. I'm baffled by the insistence in 2e that anything other than progress towards humanity is \u201cstagnation\u201d, even progress towards other goals. So we should definitely keep the \u201crefinement\u201d theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much that anything other than progress toward <i>humanity</i> is \u201cstagnation\u201d as it is that anything other than progress toward <i>no longer being a Promethean</i> isn't a Pilgrimage. I'd like to see \u201cPilgrimage\u201d be used to represent progress toward a state-change which, once achieved, renders the character something other than a Promethean, and for \u201cRefinement\u201d to refer specifically to a means of advancing Pilgrimage. (To clarify, Pilgrimage is going to be 2e's Integrity substitute.)<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that \u201cnot advancing Pilgrimage\u201d is the same as stagnation. Arguably, Promethean are <i>incapable</i> of stagnation unless and until they're able to develop a stable state, which is the sort of thing you've been talking about. It's not about transforming into something else; it's about achieving stability in what you are. Thus, a name that implies the quality of being inert (i.e., the most stable of all the chemicals) arguably fits the \u201cRefinement\u201d better than a name that implies strong reactions. In particular, the reason why aluminum is so rare in nature is because it reacts so strongly that it's almost always part of a compound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:17:06-08:00","id":840201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840197#post840197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a purely metaphysical level, I think that the problem with alternate New Dawns in Promethean, especially those that remove the weaknesses while retaining the strengths of the promethean condition is that the weaknesses derive from the strengths. The source of a Promethean's Transmutations, pseudo-immortality and all the other stuff is his Azoth, essentially a human soul burning too brightly to be contained. It is that very lack of containment that allows the promethean to work his transmutations and it is that which causes Disquiet and the Wasteland. Removing one requires removing the other. They are inseparable. A Promethean might learn new ways of accessing supernatural power, but as long as they use the Azoth, they will have to pay its price.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the game as conceived and written, you're right. But this thread is specifically about a rules hack that alters that principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:32:58-08:00","id":840207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840201#post840201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the game as conceived and written, you're right. But this thread is specifically about a rules hack that alters that principle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realise that. I wasn't trying to criticize unnecessarily. I was just trying to help. My apologies if it came out the wrong way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:42:23-08:00","id":840211,"title":"","content":"It didn't. I'm just not sure the OP is open to arguments for why the way things are makes sense. FWIW, I've got the same cognitive dissonance: animated by the Divine Fire, but not being consumed by it (Torment) or burning everything around you (Disquiet and Wasteland)? Feels like a contradiction. I'm trying to set that aside, though, because it doesn't advance the OP's goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:47:03-08:00","id":840214,"title":"","content":"I'm really liking &quot;Lumen, the refinement of Aluminum&quot;. Even if it isn't technically a refinement, I think considering it as one for the purpose of convenience/organization works fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:48:46-08:00","id":840215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840198#post840198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, the reason why aluminum is so rare in nature is because it reacts so strongly that it's almost always part of a compound.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would argue that you don't see a lot of raw Divine Fire, but instead it's found as a metaphysical &quot;compound&quot; in other aspects of the world. Unless, of course, you refine it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:59:47-08:00","id":840224,"title":"","content":"But Divine Fire is already covered by Mercurius.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a name for Vitriol, you already have it: in chemistry, vitriol is an archaic term for a sulfate; so call it Sulfur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-01-2016, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:50:54-08:00","id":840807,"title":"","content":"So, maybe it would be best to list the upsides and downsides of being a Promethean, and from whence they arise?<br /> <br /> Downsides include:<ul><li>Disquiet. Caused by the glow of the Divine Fire unnerving people. Possible solutions: Remove Divine Fire, prevent interaction of &quot;glow&quot; and people (via redirection, induced immunity, containment, or sporadic exposure).</li> <li>Wasteland. Caused by the Divine Fire scorching the land. Possible solutions: see above for Disquiet.</li> <li>Torment. Caused by unbalanced Humours/incomplete soul. Possible solutions: Complete soul. Balance Humours. Achieve Detachment (where the emotional surge does not impact rational mind and actions).</li> <li>Pandorans. Caused by radiance of the Divine Fire animating them. Possible solutions: see above for Disquiet.</li> </ul><br /> Upsides include:<ul><li>Transmutations. Caused by Pyros manipulation. Possible sources: Internal Pyros (status quo), external Pyros manipulation and reservoir, equivalent abilities (???).</li> <li>Transhuman Potential. Caused by Azoth. Possible sources: Azoth (status quo)</li> <li>Durability and &quot;Immortality&quot;. Caused by being a body animated by Azoth. Possible sources: Azoth (status quo), external animation or backup animation.</li> </ul><br /> Some method that might allow each would be a &quot;Half-Dawn&quot;, perhaps. Rather than trading Azoth for a new soul, the Promethean keeps both, shuttering the Azoth (via Athanor? Soul containment?) until needed. Another solution is to keep the Azoth, but somehow contain the emanations, redirect them somewhere &quot;harmless&quot;, or render potential assets non-interactive with the emanations (change the wavelength, as it were).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-02-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:24:28-08:00","id":841046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840807#post840807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some method that might allow each would be a &quot;Half-Dawn&quot;, perhaps. Rather than trading Azoth for a new soul, the Promethean keeps both, shuttering the Azoth (via Athanor? Soul containment?) until needed. Another solution is to keep the Azoth, but somehow contain the emanations, redirect them somewhere &quot;harmless&quot;, or render potential assets non-interactive with the emanations (change the wavelength, as it were).</div> </div> </div> </div> This could work with an idea I've been brainstorming for a &quot;Demi-Splat&quot; I'm calling &quot;Torchbearers&quot;; Prometheans who have reached a different destination on their Pilgrimage, becoming more stable than a standard Prommie, but still carry some Divine fire within them. Since the anti-transhumanist crowd keeps screaming &quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!&quot;,* how about making that fire a controlled burn?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*ALL life is fire, in a way. Living things convert food into energy by <a href=\"https://answers.yahoo.com/question/index;_ylt=AwrSbhhHn9dWvLAAhj9XNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyN2RvcnM2BGNvbG8DZ3ExBHBvcwMxBHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWMDc2M-?qid=20110522145352AAhXazN\" target=\"_blank\">metabolizing</a> it, which is basically what fire does, just slower. Also, your blood is red because it's <a href=\"https://sg.answers.yahoo.com/question/index;_ylt=AwrSbgTKntdW5XsAJVFXNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyN2RvcnM2BGNvbG8DZ3ExBHBvcwMxBHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWMDc2M-?qid=20070509121617AAATdHE\" target=\"_blank\">rusty.</a></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T19:30:20-08:00","id":841065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841046#post841046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> This could work with an idea I've been brainstorming for a &amp;quot;Demi-Splat&amp;quot; I'm calling &amp;quot;Torchbearers&amp;quot;; Prometheans who have reached a different destination on their Pilgrimage, becoming more stable than a standard Prommie, but still carry some Divine fire within them. Since the anti-transhumanist crowd keeps screaming &amp;quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!&amp;quot;,* how about making that fire a controlled burn?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*ALL life is fire, in a way. Living things convert food into energy by <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://answers.yahoo.com/question/index;_ylt=AwrSbhhHn9dWvLAAhj9XNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyN2RvcnM2BGNvbG8DZ3ExBHBvcwMxBHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWMDc2M-?qid=20110522145352AAhXazN&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">metabolizing</a> it, which is basically what fire does, just slower. Also, your blood is red because it's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://sg.answers.yahoo.com/question/index;_ylt=AwrSbgTKntdW5XsAJVFXNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyN 2RvcnM2BGNvbG8DZ3ExBHBvcwMxBHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWM Dc2M-?qid=20070509121617AAATdHE&amp;quot;]rusty</a>.[/URL]</span></div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I might have to quote your &quot;all life is fire&quot; the next time one of them tries to pull that. They use it so much I think we need a name for it- appeal to fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:45:42-08:00","id":841099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841065#post841065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I might have to quote your &quot;all life is fire&quot; the next time one of them tries to pull that.</div> </div> </div> </div>All life is transient. Most supernatural &quot;life&quot; is incapable of reproducing in any sense but the literal and exists as an implement of or testbed for thrashing entropic nightmare-systems too big to consider in more senses than the abstract and the immediate.<br /> <br /> It's decidedly impossible to manage a controlled burn for any significant length of time in the middle of an ocean of lava and battery acid that doesn't care whether the chunk of hardware floating in it stops being there because it gets out or because it gets dissolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T23:38:02-08:00","id":841162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841046#post841046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">*ALL life is fire, in a way. Living things convert food into energy by <a href=\"https://answers.yahoo.com/question/index;_ylt=AwrSbhhHn9dWvLAAhj9XNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyN2RvcnM2BGNvbG8DZ3ExBHBvcwMxBHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWMDc2M-?qid=20110522145352AAhXazN\" target=\"_blank\">metabolizing</a> it, which is basically what fire does, just slower. Also, your blood is red because it's <a href=\"https://sg.answers.yahoo.com/question/index;_ylt=AwrSbgTKntdW5XsAJVFXNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyN2RvcnM2BGNvbG8DZ3ExBHBvcwMxBHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWMDc2M-?qid=20070509121617AAATdHE\" target=\"_blank\">rusty.</a></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I said it in a different thread than this, but one of the key points to Promethean is that it takes the human condition and basically amplifies <i>everything in it</i>.<br /> <br /> So this passive burning of our normal existence runs a real risk of self-immolation for Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T23:47:39-08:00","id":841163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841162#post841162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I said it in a different thread than this, but one of the key points to Promethean is that it takes the human condition and basically amplifies <i>everything in it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that in models that correlate astrological bodies with vital organs, the Sun symbolizes the Heart.<br /> <br /> Granted, that particular bit of metaphysical anatomy doesn't <i>just</i> serve as an emotional regulator, but given that Torment derives from an imbalance of humours, there's precious few roles our intrepid Tin Men would more readily assign the big valve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T00:32:41-08:00","id":841170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841065#post841065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I might have to quote your &quot;all life is fire&quot; the next time one of them tries to pull that. They use it so much I think we need a name for it- appeal to fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm worried that you think others are &quot;trying to pull something&quot; when they are, in fact, simply enunciating the <i>core conceits</i> of the line.<br /> The implication is that they/we are trying to kind of - trick you? We're not. The book is pretty clear about these things and we tend to state it and then, you know - if we don't think someone groks, re-state it.<br /> It's very hard to gauge intent through text alone, on the webnet, so please allow me to be clear: when people say they want to have their Prometheans stay Promethean but not have the downsides of <i>being</i> Promethean, I'm not sure from what angle they're approaching the line, and my two gut reactions are<br /> 1. Maybe they don't get it?<br /> and<br /> 2. Maybe we can talk about it and I can help them kludge rules anyway.<br /> I like kludging rules!<br /> These rules are kind of hard to kludge, since it removes <i>a lot</i> of what makes the Created as they are.<br /> <br /> I mean, all life is fire; you could also make some equally-vague counter argument about it being water, or &quot;life as we know it&quot; existing in a certain spectrum of (about threeish) dimensions, but I'm not sure what any of that would actually accomplish.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of threads on the Requiem/Masquerade forum about removing Humanity or the Beast; this is like that. You don't take away a Promethean's curses/banes/condition/what-have-you - even as an alternative end-game - without changing something <i>fundamental</i> about the game.<br /> A lot of folks have strong feelings about this subject. I, for one, think it's pretty clear &quot;you can't be transhuman without first being <i>human,</i>&quot; and I think an end-goal for &quot;better than Promethean&quot; would still end with being mortal but - as I believe I posted in the other thread - opening up &quot;ex-Promethean-only&quot; merits that do, whatever it is you want.<br /> If you want to fluff it as re-harnessing the Divine Fire (even though one doesn't so much harness it as grab a live-wire and hope), that's cool.<br /> I've wanted to run a campaign for roughly forever that goes &quot;Promethean --&gt; Mortal --&gt; Mage.&quot; You don't get trans-human without having a human background, you know? It's required for the concept. Especially from a fictional characters point of view - you have to learn what it is to be human before you can surpass human.<br /> I am, of course, interested in and <i>down to clown</i> with New Dawns that result in animals, plants, fax machines; especially if it's a certain old bird getting to be a normal bird again.<br /> <br /> Other people have already asked what your refinement would add; Prometheans <i>do</i> already have the power sets to stave off the vast majority of their curses (and I've run plenty of them who use and manipulate such for selfless/selfish ends).<br /> They still have to cope with those curses, though.<br /> <br /> Earlier, you mentioned that you don't think Promethean is being true to the core story of <i>Frankenstein.</i> Would you please elaborate? I think a lot of posters feel very differently and it would be helpful (for me) to understand why you believe this/where you're coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 03-03-2016, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T00:57:19-08:00","id":841178,"title":"","content":"The &quot;All Lives are Fire&quot; thing for some reason rubbed me the wrong way the &quot;All Lives Matter&quot; rebuttal does, which got me thinking in memes, which caused this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i1236.photobucket.com/albums/ff449/ArcaneArtsCreativeStudios/Promethean%20Sentiment_zpsigrvxxur.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At least, that's how I imagine a Promethean would respond to the sentiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T04:16:16-08:00","id":841215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=840197#post840197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a purely metaphysical level, I think that the problem with alternate New Dawns in Promethean, especially those that remove the weaknesses while retaining the strengths of the promethean condition is that the weaknesses derive from the strengths. The source of a Promethean's Transmutations, pseudo-immortality and all the other stuff is his Azoth, essentially a human soul burning too brightly to be contained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. So where would you stand on a &quot;New Dawn&quot; where you shed the Promethean weaknesses, but become limited in the strengths? Effectively Azoth 0, you keep the Transmutations you have, but can't get any more (after all, if you're perfected, that precludes getting any better), and you need an external alembic to hold your Pyros (because it will burn you now).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841046#post841046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the anti-transhumanist crowd keeps screaming &quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!&quot;,* how about making that fire a controlled burn?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think Mortality is?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:23:07-08:00","id":841308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841162#post841162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I said it in a different thread than this, but one of the key points to Promethean is that it takes the human condition and basically amplifies <i>everything in it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that kind of the point of every game line? You take parts of the human existance and amplify it? That was my impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:23:25-08:00","id":841309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841215#post841215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. So where would you stand on a &quot;New Dawn&quot; where you shed the Promethean weaknesses, but become limited in the strengths? Effectively Azoth 0, you keep the Transmutations you have, but can't get any more (after all, if you're perfected, that precludes getting any better), and you need an external alembic to hold your Pyros (because it will burn you now).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds pretty good. I've actually played a game in which the we (the players) basically managed to get a cabal of mages to place our Azoth in a Phylactery, which meant that Disquiet and the Wasteland were both centred around that and we could still access our Transmutations and so on, albeit at a penalty depending on how far away the Phylactery was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:36:47-08:00","id":841316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841170#post841170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very hard to gauge intent through text alone, on the webnet, so please allow me to be clear: when people say they want to have their Prometheans stay Promethean but not have the downsides of <i>being</i> Promethean, I'm not sure from what angle they're approaching the line, and my two gut reactions are<br /> 1. Maybe they don't get it?<br /> and<br /> 2. Maybe we can talk about it and I can help them kludge rules anyway.<br /> I like kludging rules!<br /> These rules are kind of hard to kludge, since it removes <i>a lot</i> of what makes the Created as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't wish to give offense, but I legitimately cannot trace or understand the origin of this line of thinking. A lot of people liked it, clearly, but I think a lot of people are maybe just liking anything that says &quot;no transhumanism&quot; at this point because this thread for some reason is irresistible to them. One of the things I personally like about the Chronicles of Darkness is that it's so okay with heresy not only does it refuse the concept of canon and translate everything into vague and often repeatedly-retold Just-So stories, chatroom rumors, or scribbled diaries written by the mad, it actually once went so far as to publish an actual book called Blasphemies for the express purpose of ENCOURAGING this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> But you're saying that in a thread where the OP has repeatedly and in no uncertain terms outlined their desire and intention, you were unsure of either their desire and intention and defaulted to the assumption that THEY didn't understand what they were reading? I think there's something incredibly insulting about that. It bothers me that your sentiment is the one people are joining their thumbs-up voice with. It bothers me a lot, actually. But my impression is that there's a sanction here for telling OP this whole thing is wrong as long as you abstract it a little. I think Promethean is a great story and very cool, but I also think ripping its guts out to feed your dreams on is totally fine and those stories can also be great and very cool.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the idea that it is in any sense difficult to &quot;kludge&quot; is the one I think it's going to actually be productive to deal with.<br /> <br /> It is incredibly easy to homebrew template elements in the Chronicles of Darkness, because they're only conceptually interrelated and those concepts are easily rewritten.<br /> <br /> Let's take it for granted that being mortal is pretty lame in a world where everyone knows someone who disappeared into the night. In fact even Promethean 1E understands this, offering vague suggestions of superhumanity (TRANShumanity, even?) and uncertain boons for those who complete their Pilgrimage as incentive. The writers were certainly conscious that &quot;give up your awesome powers in exchange for not scaring the children so much&quot; wasn't going to be an easy sell for everyone. So, okay. Screw that whole thing. So you have to kludge something different. I propose that this is not difficult.<br /> <br /> You've got some obvious drawbacks (Disquiet, Wastelands, Torment) and you've got the idea of the Divine Fire. Let's say that those bad things only happen because demiurges are crap at making Prometheans and they express Azoth imperfectly by nature, sort of like how a red strobelight is freaky even though there's nothing wrong with the lightbulb inside. So a Refinement, Lumium or whatever, that shapes you (spiritually and perhaps physically) to refine your channeling mechanisms to alleviate the bad stuff, the strobe effect as it were. Shine purely. Going with the OP's desire for human connection and the guardian angel idea, let's actually reverse the equation and say you can cause a kind of Disquiet that makes people look to you as a leader and trust you inherently - if you want tradeoffs, and OP mentioned they do, they also get really good at reading you and you still can't turn it off, so people are ALWAYS trusting you and looking to you as a leader. You can create Wastelands that frighten and eventually burn things in Twilight - but indiscriminately, so you end up with clean, modern, spiritually-dead towns that, lacking the usual &quot;immune system&quot; of a spiritual ecology, rely on you to defend and are somewhat more vulnerable to physical things moving in. Rather than Torment, you enter creative fugues where you are driven to build and refine Great Works, possibly that produce small measures of Vitriol, but these things draw Pandorans like a lighthouse and often demand rare and dangerous components SOMEONE has to go and get before they can get down to business and ride out the compulsion.<br /> <br /> How's that look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:42:46-08:00","id":841324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841316#post841316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you're saying that in a thread where the OP has repeatedly and in no uncertain terms outlined their desire and intention, you were unsure of either their desire and intention and defaulted to the assumption that THEY didn't understand what they were reading?</div> </div> </div> </div>OP believes the assimilationist reading to be an accurate description of Promethean's intended presentation and has on multiple occasions demonstrated the misapprehension that the Created are innately immortal. There's a fairly thick line between just not liking the material and actively misreading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:49:31-08:00","id":841330,"title":"","content":"You know, I asked two pages back what you needed, OP. I STILL haven't gotten an answer. You have the themes you want. You have affinity Transmutations. You've even suggested some Milestones, though nothing formal (and Milestones tend to be personalized anyways). <i>What is left to do?</i> So far, the only thing I've seen you work on are stereotypes and a name. Which, frankly speaking, are kinda meaningless. Fun to read, people enjoy them, but don't actually add to the game at all. <br /> <br /> I'm not going to tell you what you should or should not do. But, so far, my impression is that you seem to be focused on <i>rejection</i> and the negatives rather than building something up. You're defining this idea by what its not. And I believe that's the source of all the thread issues here. Forums seem to react against something they percieve as an attack on their views of what's good and right. *cough*mageforums*cough*<br /> <br /> I think we'll get some better ideas and work if we get some solid ideas of where you want to go instead of you telling us where you don't want to go. Even your stereotypes seem to focus on mocking other Refinements for going human instead of praising whatever their end goal actually is. You don't like how at least some alchemists are antagonistic - I find this rather strange considering that the details we have are so scarce as to be practically non-existant. Maybe they antagonistic ones are all just affected by Disquiet, which is something you are not considering with your Refinement either. You are rejecting the relationship without details. We don't know what they're all like as a whole. <br /> <br /> What is this project about? What is your end goal in concrete terms? What form does your balanced burn take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:07:37-08:00","id":841338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841316#post841316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wish to give offense, but I legitimately cannot trace or understand the origin of this line of thinking. A lot of people liked it, clearly, but I think a lot of people are maybe just liking anything that says &quot;no transhumanism&quot; at this point because this thread for some reason is irresistible to them. One of the things I personally like about the Chronicles of Darkness is that it's so okay with heresy not only does it refuse the concept of canon and translate everything into vague and often repeatedly-retold Just-So stories, chatroom rumors, or scribbled diaries written by the mad, it actually once went so far as to publish an actual book called Blasphemies for the express purpose of ENCOURAGING this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> But you're saying that in a thread where the OP has repeatedly and in no uncertain terms outlined their desire and intention, you were unsure of either their desire and intention and defaulted to the assumption that THEY didn't understand what they were reading? I think there's something incredibly insulting about that. It bothers me that your sentiment is the one people are joining their thumbs-up voice with. It bothers me a lot, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div> Welcome to the forums.[/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> Not that long ago, someone posted a thread in Mage about how to change the Seers to make them less black hat. I created a fairly lengthy attempt at some suggestions. And, what happened? People were telling me NO, NO, YOU ARE WRONG! THAT IS NOT SEER! I was all like, &quot;That's kinda the point?&quot; And then excuses were thrown around for the aggressive behaviors. &quot;Oh, we're just really in love with the game, and we just want to protect it!&quot;<br /> <br /> My problem with the OP are three fold. First, and most pressing, is that he or she is not giving us any hint as to what they really want other than some vague &quot;trans-Promethan evolution.&quot; That's something that's huge in the Ordo Dracul - they constantly argue about what the end goal of their Transcendance is. Its a huge social plot hook. Which is great for vampire, which is primarily a social game. That's the point of it. In Promethean, which is a game about spiritual journeys in the first place, doesn't benefit from social plot hooks. It benefits from clarity of purpose. I don't see that. <br /> <br /> The OP also seems to be making some assumptions about how Alchemists, Vitrol, and some other parts of the Pilgrimage work, which I find to be a bit strange, but sadly standard fare for the forums - the assumptions flying around about Mage and Changeling are just as thick (well, less so Changeling now that we have a good chunk of the rules).<br /> <br /> And what about switching Refinements? Refinement swapping is a thing. Its meant to be a feature. How does this single Refinement mesh with the others?<br /> <br /> There's a lot of critiquing that can happen here. And rightfully so - if you want to say that all life is fire? Then you should be aware that your ideas need to be Refined and forged as well. Outright telling someone they shouldn't do something isn't quite right. But neither is protecting an idea from all criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-03-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:37:40-08:00","id":841352,"title":"","content":"If the problem is that the Divine Fire is basically the mystical equivalent to Naquadria, why not just get rid of it entirely? No Azoth. No Pyros. The following Spheres are probably what you need to create a non-DF based Promethean: Spirit, Mind, Prime, and either Matter or Life depending on the model. If you want a purely digital character who exists as software inside computer systems, you can get rid of the Matter or Life and use Forces instead. With sufficient levels of Prime, you can make the body you use as an anchor for this new Pattern into a mobile node that generates its own Quintessence. Build as a Mage. Take spells that mimic the effects of whatever Promethean powers you want. Replace Disquiet, Wastelands, and Firestorms with whatever Paradox Flaws you find to be appropriate. (Hell, maybe those things ARE paradox flaws.) If you want to duplicate the effect of Azothic Radiance, that's probably Prime + Mind. Arrange a permanent working or two to give yourself the passive benefits of being Promethean (resilience, heal via electricity, etc). Your paradigm? &quot;I'm a Promethean.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 03-03-2016, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T10:05:50-08:00","id":841369,"title":"","content":"Granted, we have some kneejerking to deal with, but it is actually fine if someone wants to play transhumanist Promethean. Do what's fun.<br /> <br /> It's trying to justify it beyond &quot;That's what I want to do with my game&quot;, particularly with poorly thought out responses like &quot;All lives are fire&quot;, that's going to get my goat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T12:21:15-08:00","id":841430,"title":"","content":"Which, to be fair, is probably just as much a result of the polarization that's going on here. We're pushing each other to the extremes, which creates exaggerated responces on both ends. I think we're all just taking this a little bit too seriously. There's no reason for anyone's goat to be gotten. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think that being human is awesome. There's <i>soooo</i> much potential in every human soul. And that's before we touch on magical immortality and psychic powers that a Refined soul will likely have access to. Sure, humans are flawed beings, and we fail a lot. As a cop, I see a lot of it every day. But I also see a lot of good that people do, and what we can acomplish together. The point of the transhumanist movement isn't to make us something inhuman. Its to make us Human+. Or H+. Better humans, but still very much human. I feel that its completely within theme for a Promethean to end up as an Integrity 10 immortal human with superior physical, mental, and mystical capabilities. But I also think its part of the game already. <br /> <br /> Of course, I think everyone here is familar with the idea that I don't run things according to most books. I detest D&amp;Disms that slip into the games, I come up with homebrew personal theories, like the Mortal+ / Predator / Magical Being / Soul Forger / Creationism axis of supernaturals, and using it to create things like &quot;The Supernal Realms are actually all part of Faerie that got conquered by mortals.&quot; Or blood working as iron. Or the Midnight Games, where the antagonism between Fang and Fur is the result of sportsmanship rivalry, and the Caspers are dedicated to win back the city championship from the Potters this season, come hell or high water. So, I have to be very careful with what I say and double check facts. My views of what the CofD should be are definitely non-standard. I don't think it would be well recieved if I started talking about how Geist is as much of a spiritual game as Promethean, and how the eight Archetypes are really the same 5+unaligned+2*antagonists formula that almost all other games use.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the point I'm trying to make is that inflamitory statements, which do come from both sides on here, aren't helping anyone. Its driving everyone to extremes and we need to have constructive conversations here. Or at least we should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T13:18:41-08:00","id":841465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841369#post841369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, we have some kneejerking to deal with, but it is actually fine if someone wants to play transhumanist Promethean. Do what's fun.<br /> <br /> It's trying to justify it beyond &quot;That's what I want to do with my game&quot;, particularly with poorly thought out responses like &quot;All lives are fire&quot;, that's going to get my goat.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have \u200bseen &quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!!!!&quot; used to threadcrap SO many times, I felt we needed a response. We all understand the fire metaphor. The horse is dead. Now you're just punching a bottle of glue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T14:22:31-08:00","id":841497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841316#post841316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't wish to give offense, but I legitimately cannot trace or understand the origin of this line of thinking. A lot of people liked it, clearly, but I think a lot of people are maybe just liking anything that says &quot;no transhumanism&quot; at this point because this thread for some reason is irresistible to them. One of the things I personally like about the Chronicles of Darkness is that it's so okay with heresy not only does it refuse the concept of canon and translate everything into vague and often repeatedly-retold Just-So stories, chatroom rumors, or scribbled diaries written by the mad, it actually once went so far as to publish an actual book called Blasphemies for the express purpose of ENCOURAGING this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> But you're saying that in a thread where the OP has repeatedly and in no uncertain terms outlined their desire and intention, you were unsure of either their desire and intention and defaulted to the assumption that THEY didn't understand what they were reading? I think there's something incredibly insulting about that. It bothers me that your sentiment is the one people are joining their thumbs-up voice with. It bothers me a lot, actually. But my impression is that there's a sanction here for telling OP this whole thing is wrong as long as you abstract it a little. I think Promethean is a great story and very cool, but I also think ripping its guts out to feed your dreams on is totally fine and those stories can also be great and very cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of proved my point about the &quot;words on the internet&quot; thing - my intention has been missed.<br /> What I was trying to say was a positive thing - you cannot, really, change something until you understand it.<br /> <br /> People misread things! It happens. I am trying to be positive, to allow that maybe there was a break in the logic of the reader, not because I am being an asshole (you will know when I am being an asshole, as the post will be deleted and replaced with &quot;sorry, needed coffee&quot;) but because I want to understand why people are wanting this.<br /> These themes (transhumanity, which is <i>not</i> superhumanity, I wan to make that <i>abundantly</i> clear) which are very much opposed to Promethean - or at least, not within Promethean's intention, scope and <i>mindset</i> - are not going to be easy to put in, or reconcile with the game.<br /> I'm also aware that, from this side of the argument, there's likely some feelings that transhumnanity &quot;shits all over the Promethean we love.&quot; <br /> Not to be derisive, but it kind of does, which is why I wonder to myself <i>did they not get it?</i> Moving towards being a better Promethean instead of being mortal kind of, vastly changes the game.<br /> <br /> You say &quot;repeatedly and in no uncertain terms&quot; but I <i>really</i> don't feel that way. Otherwise, I wouldn't have posted this, and then asked for what his interpretation of <i>Frankenstein</i> was so I could better understand <i>from where he is coming</i> in order to <i>make suggestions that could help</i>.<br /> <br /> People are going to run transhumanist Promethean, I'm pretty sure everyone here who has said some variation of &quot;ew&quot; is aware of that.<br /> This is about that &quot;did they get it&quot; part, though - you cannot <i>fundamentally change a thing</i> without first showing clear and correct <i>understanding</i> of the thing, and sometimes I worry about that.<br /> Didn't the Daemon in <i>Frankenstein</i> basically beg to join humanity and rage when he was rejected? Becoming human, man. Gotta understand it first.<br /> <br /> As for heresy - yes, I agree! Make things that are <i>blasphemous</i>. I <i>loved LOVED</i> the Hundred-Handred Refinement in 1e as a thing Prometheans who are sick or disillusioned with the Pilgrimage hop onto, and I will - unless the 2e version is <i>amazing</i> - likely run it as that.<br /> I wouldn't call that trans-human, though, I'd call that - well, you can be a monster or a <i>monster</i>.<br /> I really, really think that the trans-human aspect of Promethean is found after <i>becoming</i> human.<br /> <br /> Tangentially, if you want to run Prometheans who are &quot;making their own Pilgrimage&quot; - why do you even <i>need</i> a new Refinement, is a thought I keep coming back to.<br /> 1. Provide easy access to the Disquiet/Wasteland mitigating Transmutations<br /> 2. Play around with Pandoran Transmutations<br /> 3. Allow custom Transmutations or power combinations (I cannot rightly recall their name, at the moment) which make those reductions easier to activate/maintain but at a price (harder to resist low Disquiet but can't progress to 3; Wastelands start sooner; caps to Pilgrimage Trait).<br /> Those are much easier to fit in and - this is important, I think - they provide room for PCs who are <i>on</i> the Pilgrimage to take them, and they also provide antagonist fodder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841316#post841316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the idea that it is in any sense difficult to &quot;kludge&quot; is the one I think it's going to actually be productive to deal with.<br /> <br /> It is incredibly easy to homebrew template elements in the Chronicles of Darkness, because they're only conceptually interrelated and those concepts are easily rewritten.<br /> <br /> Let's take it for granted that being mortal is pretty lame in a world where everyone knows someone who disappeared into the night. In fact even Promethean 1E understands this, offering vague suggestions of superhumanity (TRANShumanity, even?) and uncertain boons for those who complete their Pilgrimage as incentive. The writers were certainly conscious that &quot;give up your awesome powers in exchange for not scaring the children so much&quot; wasn't going to be an easy sell for everyone. So, okay. Screw that whole thing. So you have to kludge something different. I propose that this is not difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>We already live in a world where everyone knows someone who disappeared into the night. Why would you want to have that be something that happens (because being a Vampire or Promethean or Mage is <i>so safe</i>) <i>on top of</i> having, you know, horrible never-ending curses?<br /> Promethean offers an out.<br /> Again, I understand wanting to play around with super-powers and be more than human.<br /> I guess I just don't understand the obsession with changing a horror game to do this. I try to understand it, but - and I mean this in a very positive way - I encourage people to instead burn down (haha, ha, ha) the Promethean they don't like and build back up the thing they want.<br /> If you end up with a bunch of super-corpses throwing around crazy super-powers and laughing about how much better they are than humanity, though, then that's a pretty far fall from both Promethean and <i>Frankenstein.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841316#post841316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got some obvious drawbacks (Disquiet, Wastelands, Torment) and you've got the idea of the Divine Fire. Let's say that those bad things only happen because demiurges are crap at making Prometheans and they express Azoth imperfectly by nature, sort of like how a red strobelight is freaky even though there's nothing wrong with the lightbulb inside. So a Refinement, Lumium or whatever, that shapes you (spiritually and perhaps physically) to refine your channeling mechanisms to alleviate the bad stuff, the strobe effect as it were. Shine purely. Going with the OP's desire for human connection and the guardian angel idea, let's actually reverse the equation and say you can cause a kind of Disquiet that makes people look to you as a leader and trust you inherently - if you want tradeoffs, and OP mentioned they do, they also get really good at reading you and you still can't turn it off, so people are ALWAYS trusting you and looking to you as a leader. You can create Wastelands that frighten and eventually burn things in Twilight - but indiscriminately, so you end up with clean, modern, spiritually-dead towns that, lacking the usual &quot;immune system&quot; of a spiritual ecology, rely on you to defend and are somewhat more vulnerable to physical things moving in. Rather than Torment, you enter creative fugues where you are driven to build and refine Great Works, possibly that produce small measures of Vitriol, but these things draw Pandorans like a lighthouse and often demand rare and dangerous components SOMEONE has to go and get before they can get down to business and ride out the compulsion.<br /> <br /> How's that look?</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks pretty bad, honestly.<br /> First, you've changed the core conceit in such a way that now it fits a new refinement based on staying Promethean, but you'd have to re-jigger the <i>rest</i> of the Refinements to fit fully in this new core setting.<br /> Second, you have a &quot;drawback&quot; where you get free minions in a game that is predominately not designed Cults, so I'm not sure what powers you'll write-in to fit that new paradigm, since Prometheans already <i>have</i> a baker's dozen powers that re-write or mitigate their drawbacks. What would mitigate this one? Make it so people <i>don't</i> see you as a leader - bring you back to the baseline?<br /> Also, Disquiet itself is designed to build up to a an explosion that results in either Torment or the Promethean getting chased out, or fleeing, or <i>some</i> kind of forward-momentum action. This just builds up to you having a bunch of dudes who would always follow you? There's no release there.<br /> You mentioned that instead of Torment you'd have a fugue-state where you'd build and refine great works, but I've no idea what you mean by this - like crafting Athanors? Like being forced to do things that are beneficial? What would they try to make?<br /> <br /> You've also kludged approximately 0 mechanics, here. What will these <i>look like</i>. What will the new Conditions be. How will they interact with - or, as seems to be the case, replace - the existing rules, and how severe will they be? Are you going to just replace words and ideas in already-established systems or write up new ones? Most importantly, what kind of powers are you going to make that replace the ones these render obsolete - and, if intending to run these alongside each other in the same setting, what will you do to balance them together, and what changes are necessary to other parts of the Pilgrimage because of these new powers?<br /> <br /> Look, this post has already become very, very long. If anybody wants to discuss this thread with me, just PM me. I'll be around to critique mechanics and try to offer alternatives.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T14:24:57-08:00","id":841498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841465#post841465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have \u200bseen &quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!!!!&quot; used to threadcrap SO many times, I felt we needed a response. We all understand the fire metaphor. The horse is dead. Now you're just punching a bottle of glue.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of punching a dead horse, I find it kind of worth mentioning that it is <i>not a metaphor</i>. Prometheans are <i>literally</i> on fire and it is <i>literally</i> slowly killing them, the land around them, and the metaphysical/inter-personal relationships they make with humanity.<br /> Without the fire, they cease to be; with the fire, everything degrades.<br /> You have to either work <i>within</i> that conceit to make a Promethean who wants to be &quot;better than Promethean&quot; or &quot;not human,&quot; or else change it entirely (which is a long rewrite, I'd imagine).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T14:55:34-08:00","id":841517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841465#post841465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have \u200bseen &quot;YOU ARE ON FIRE!!!!&quot; used to threadcrap SO many times, I felt we needed a response. We all understand the fire metaphor. The horse is dead. Now you're just punching a bottle of glue.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, because many of us feel the same way about trying to argue transhumanism for Promethean.<br /> <br /> That aside, it also doesn't change the fact that, yes, Prometheans are on fire. Any attempt to shift the humanist nature of the game to a transhumanist one has to address how to handle the fact the Prometheans are on fire and what to do about.<br /> <br /> The best part for the transhumanist Promethean argument is that below either transhumanism or humanism, there is the idea of focusing destructive energies to produce a creative force. Fire will devour anything until you focus it. If you want to make a case for transhumanism, you can, but it has to be something where the fire is doing something. Stagnation means you burn out. You cannot remain a Promethean without burning out.<br /> <br /> If you want to reinvent the game, you have to keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> You'll notice Wyrdhamster has a Alternative New Dawn thread that I haven't touched. There's a reason for that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, while it might be irritating for us to point out the point that &quot;you are on fire&quot; is a big ass part of the game, &quot;All Lives are Fire&quot; is such a failed counterpoint is' ridiculous. It's easier for you to just say 'We know, we don't care.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, you can say you don't care. I actually dropped this thread when Gecko made it clear he doesn't care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-03-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T17:06:48-08:00","id":841587,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sadly necessary postscript: Please please please don't come into this thread to argue over whether or not it should be a thing. There are several threads for arguing over the Pilgrimage. This is for working on homebrew.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm really sad and disappointed that this turned into yet another argument honestly<br /> <br /> There are multiple threads for that<br /> <br /> This is literally only for working out a homebrew thing that some people thought would be fun<br /> <br /> I remember making a thread about alternatives to Kindred of the East, homebrewing Cainite Clans for Asia, where I briefly said in the intro &quot;this isn't a thread for people to argue over whether or not KotE was good or not, this is just for people who want alternatives&quot;. And guess what? No one came in and started arguing with us to defend KotE! We were able to have a very productive and entertaining conversation about homebrew Clans! It was great! I guess that gave me false hope that people understood the meaning of &quot;there are already multiple threads for arguing about this subject please just go there&quot;.<br /> <br /> All of the recent...discourse on Promethean has actually inspired me to start working on a larger-scale setting/theme/mechanics hack for Promethean. I'm waiting for 2e to come out fully so I can sort of experience it all at once and see what I want to change or add. I'll post a dev thread then so we can work on it. The main goal of the thing is to make it truer to its source material, Frankenstein in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 03-03-2016, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T19:27:54-08:00","id":841660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841497#post841497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kind of proved my point about the &quot;words on the internet&quot; thing - my intention has been missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bluntly, I'm unwilling to give you or ArcaneArts or whoever else has been primarily focused on insisting this is all BadWrongFun the benefit of the doubt. There's a difference between loving a thing and trying to bludgeon someone else to silence because they don't love it the same way you do. Onyx Path has been really...really awesome about taking a stand on that. I don't love everything they do (admittedly I do love most of it); sometimes I don't love a particular thing a LOT. But I love what they try to do and what they stand for in the industry, in particular their open embrace of breaks with tradition, mutation, mutilation, recreation, all the myriad and violent shades of creativity. Sometimes, the community stands with them on that.<br /> <br /> Not this time. Super lame, guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T20:00:18-08:00","id":841668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841517#post841517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny, because many of us feel the same way about trying to argue transhumanism for Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then maybe just stay out of threads about Transhumanism. All due respect; at this point, your involvement is toxic. Go spread Disquiet somewhere else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fire will devour anything until you focus it. If you want to make a case for transhumanism, you can, but it has to be something where the fire is doing something. </div> </div> </div>Now THIS has potential. My earlier idea of &quot;Torchbearers&quot; has a flaw; torches are consumed by the flames, and easily set fire to things around them. So maybe something that harnesses fire for positive ends? Like...a lantern? And drawing from Greek stories again, I have a new idea:<br /> <br /> A goal for Prometheans (and maybe Alchemists) to strive for, one in which the Divine fire acts as guiding light, rather than a destructive blaze. Seeking a new path forward, not just for themselves, but perhaps all mankind as well. And so, might I suggest...Diogenoi? After the ancient Greek philosopher, Diogenes of Sinope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 03-03-2016, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T20:17:41-08:00","id":841674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841660#post841660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bluntly, I'm unwilling to give you or ArcaneArts or whoever else has been primarily focused on insisting this is all BadWrongFun the benefit of the doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, this \u201cUs vs. Them\u201d mentality is a big part of the problem; there have been efforts by those who find the topic distasteful to provide constructive feedback <i>despite</i> that; and telling them to shut up and get out poisons the atmosphere. For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841660#post841660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between loving a thing and trying to bludgeon someone else to silence because they don't love it the same way you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not characterize Ben's posts as bludgeoning someone into silence. Rather, I would characterize it as an attempt to find <i>some</i> sort of common ground so that something constructive can be done. That involves trying to find a way to express what the OP is going for in terms that make sense to one's own understanding of the game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I had a Sig on the old forums. When we switched to the new forums, I didn't brother of reconstruct it \u2014 and now I'm using my Sig-space for other purposes. But given what's been happening here, I think I need to resurrect it just this one time:<br /> <br /> The essentials for a productive discussion: <br /> <b>\u2022 Tact:</b> Be friendly, helpful, and cooperative. <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Candor:</b> Be frank and sincere. <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Intelligence:</b> Think before you speak. <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Goodwill:</b> Reasonable people can disagree. <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Reception:</b> Listen to what others are saying, not to what you <i>think</i> they're saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-04-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T20:18:44-08:00","id":841675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841587#post841587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is for working on homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precious little of that seems to have actually occurred apart from deciding that Ferrum was the Swole Refinement and that &quot;Stannum&quot; means &quot;Destroy All Humans&quot; as far as this hypothetical Refinement is concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm really sad and disappointed that this turned into yet another argument honestly [\u2026] This is literally only for working out a homebrew thing that some people thought would be fun </div> </div> </div>You kind of dropped the ball on that when you took time out of the thread to directly encourage someone to build a pointless and nonsensical &quot;counterargument&quot; for a fairly literal analogy that has been brought up in the face of the question of Why Can't Ulgan Stabilize that people seem to keep missing.<br /> <br /> If you want to make homebrew, <i>make the damn homebrew.</i> Twain it up and Omit Needless Words if you're concerned about threadcrapping \u2014 the Flag button is there for a reason. You want the thread to stay focused? <i>Focus.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T20:38:09-08:00","id":841679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841675#post841675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precious little of that seems to have actually occurred apart from deciding that Ferrum was the Swole Refinement and that &quot;Stannum&quot; means &quot;Destroy All Humans&quot; as far as this hypothetical Refinement is concerned.<br /> <br /> You kind of dropped the ball on that when you took time out of the thread to directly encourage someone to build a pointless and nonsensical &quot;counterargument&quot; for a fairly literal analogy that has been brought up in the face of the question of Why Can't Ulgan Stabilize that people seem to keep missing.<br /> <br /> If you want to make homebrew, <i>make the damn homebrew.</i> Twain it up and Omit Needless Words if you're concerned about threadcrapping \u2014 the Flag button is there for a reason. You want the thread to stay focused? <i>Focus.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying I deserve to be threadcrapped because I didn't do a good job of staying focused on my own thread? <br /> <br /> And by the way? Do you want to know why the counter argument came up? Because people who didn't like the premise of the thread showed up and started threadcrapping! Literally the first responses this thread got were attempts to argue! A mod had to step in multiple times! Hell, some of the people who were arguing actually apologized and said they wouldn't do it again- but they came back! Just stop! Let it be! I don't care if you make a thread that's literally called &quot;geckopirateship sucks&quot; or &quot;transhumanism is garbage&quot; to complain about things. If you want to argue, use the threads where people are arguing! For gods sake, please, just...stop. <br /> <br /> You know why I haven't used the flag button? Because I didn't think I needed to. Because I thought people here knew better and I didn't want to make work for the mods.<br /> <br /> Okay, let's move forward: no more argument. I will flag any threadcrapping. If you support me, please don't try to counterargue, either. Just ignore them. If you want to wade into The Discourse, as I've mentioned before, there are multiple threads to fight about frankensteins and humanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 03-03-2016, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T20:40:53-08:00","id":841681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=841679#post841679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying I deserve to be threadcrapped because I didn't do a good job of staying focused on my own thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying, as someone who has been in arguments that have lasted months and years, that entering a back-and-forth wastes more space and time than reporting a threadcrap and moving on.<br /> <br /> Move on. I seem to recall something about an idea for a Transmutation messing with Vitriol?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T20:44:45-08:00","id":841686,"title":"","content":"Not sure how &quot;please don't use this thread for argument&quot; counts as a back and forth but okay, whatever, I agree that back and forths are bad. <br /> <br /> The Vitriol connection was related to the connection between the Lumen and alchemists. The 2e preview for alchemists says that they need Vitriol for permanent alterations to their own bodies, and since the Lumen would be willing to provide them with it it made sense to give them Transmutations based on controlling and even generating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/av